WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:02.500
"Life moves pretty fast.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:07.920
If you don't stop and look around once in
a while, you could miss it."

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.960
Well, Ferris Bueller's Day Off moves pretty
fast, too.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:15.100
Perhaps everyone has seen it so many times
that they didn't stop and look around and

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.620
realize that there are a lot of baffling events
in the movie.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.960
One of Ferris’ earliest schemes involves
securing a car for the day.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.160
Ferris tells us

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:26.820
"I asked for a car, I got a computer."

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.180
...as a way of explaining why he doesn’t
have wheels of his own.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:35.380
The problem is that his computer is one of
the many expensive toys that fill his bedroom.

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:40.050
In addition to a computer cool enough to be
connected to the web in the mid-80s, Ferris'

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:45.210
room is also stuffed with a slick sound system
and even a synthesizer he puts to particularly

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:45.720
good use.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:54.239
Throw in the classic electric guitar and he's
got quite a bit of money laying around.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:55.300
Sell your stuff, Bueller!

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:00.739
After fooling his parents with a fake illness,
Ferris' next big task is convincing his best

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:03.360
friend Cameron Frye to join him on his day
off.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:07.700
Ironically, Cameron is already out of school
for the day, home sick in bed for real.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:11.160
Ferris doesn't believe Cameron, noting his
hypochondriac

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:11.880
tendencies.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:16.380
But Cameron does seem to be quite ill, so
much so that he barely feels like moving.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:21.100
Somehow, Ferris is able to rouse him and bring
him along on the trip, and just like that,

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:21.820
Cameron is fine.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:25.680
He goes from lying in bed to hanging out at
a Chicago Cubs game.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:30.380
Not once during the day do we see Cameron
becoming dizzy, trying to nap, or knocking

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:31.260
back some DayQuil.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:34.540
He was either faking it, or he was miraculously
cured.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.960
Ferris invites Cameron along, in part, because
he needs a car.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:42.220
They could just use Cameron's, but Ferris
is too greedy for that.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:47.040
He wants to spend his day on the town in style,
and has his heart set on stealing Cameron’s

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.660
father’s car: A limited edition 1961 Ferrari
convertible.

00:01:51.109 --> 00:01:55.079
It's a pretty sweet ride, and so valuable
that Cameron’s Dad doesn't even drive it.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.000
"He just rubs it with a diaper."

00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:00.940
Despite the car’s value, though, there’s
little to no security for it.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:05.279
It's just sitting there, without any protection,
in the garage, which Cameron and Ferris can

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.140
just walk into.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:08.940
It's almost as if Mr. Frye wants it to get
stolen.

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:14.380
Ferris covers his tracks at his house with
a dummy, a complex pulley system, and a tape

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:15.700
playing snoring sounds.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:19.990
By comparison, his scheme to get his girlfriend,
Sloane Peterson, out of school for the day

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:21.500
is surprisingly low-tech.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:25.680
It starts with a phone call from Cameron posing
as Sloane's father, claiming her grandmother

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:26.200
died.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.920
Ferris and Cameron then head to the school
to grab Sloane.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:34.150
When Ferris arrives, he has to disguise himself
as her father by wearing an oversized trench

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:35.560
coat and old-fashioned hat.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:40.820
Somehow dean of students Mr. Rooney is fooled
by the lazy ruse, even after Ferris and Sloane

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:42.160
share a long, wet kiss.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:47.460
One of the first things Ferris does on his
day off is take Cameron and Sloane to an extremely

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.460
fancy restaurant.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:53.020
He doesn’t have a reservation, so he steals
someone else's from the restaurant’s list.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:55.540
For this scheme, he chooses to pose as Abe
Froman:

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:57.560
"The Sausage King of Chicago."

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.360
The restaurant’s host is, of course, extremely
skeptical of Ferris' claim.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:05.920
Ferris works around him by having Sloane call
the restaurant and describe him as Froman.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:10.480
Somehow, it works, and the baby-faced teen
who is obviously not a meat magnate gets his

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:10.980
table.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:15.840
One of the most famous scenes in Ferris Bueller's
Day Off is the parade sequence, but there's

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:18.100
a lot about the scene that’s hard to understand.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:22.540
It's a big cultural event that shuts down
several downtown city blocks, but it's somehow

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.400
held in the middle of a weekday.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.430
The heart of the scene is a bit baffling,
too.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:31.170
Huge parades are highly secured, but this
one just lets some random teen up onto a float

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.470
to lip-sync to an old Wayne Newton song?

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:35.940
And why does the float have a microphone anyway?

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:38.320
It's not hooked up to any kind of sound system.

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:42.040
This all leads to a synchronized dance number
set to "Twist and Shout."

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:45.570
It's a little more realistic that Ferris would
know that song, but it's not realistic at

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:49.630
all that a bunch of people have put together
dance routines to go along with this otherwise

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:51.380
completely spontaneous performance.

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:55.680
Ferris plans his day off so it’s packed
with extremely fun activities.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:04:00.620
He and his friends go to the Sears Tower,
the Art Institute of Chicago, a fancy lunch,

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:02.920
a Chicago Cubs game, and even a parade.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:07.250
One problem with packing all that into one
day is that there's no way Ferris, Cameron,

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:10.200
and Sloane could fit it all in with the limited
time they've got.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:14.870
It's mid-morning by the time Ferris convinces
Cameron to come with him, then he has to jailbreak

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:17.420
Sloane from school, and then drive into the
city.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:20.060
Once they're in the city, they have to leave
the car in a garage.

00:04:20.249 --> 00:04:25.279
Factoring in travel time between activities,
plus setbacks like traffic, there's no way

00:04:25.279 --> 00:04:27.970
Ferris is getting back to the suburbs before
his parents.

00:04:28.999 --> 00:04:33.360
The villain of the film is dean of students
Ed Rooney, and he both hates and obsesses

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:34.540
over Ferris Bueller.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:38.300
The thing is that Rooney actually has a good
reason, noting that Ferris...

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:40.600
"He gives good kids bad ideas."

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:45.200
It's Rooney's job to keep the student body
in line and in class, something Ferris doesn't

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:45.700
help with.

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:48.180
He has so many absences that it's a problem.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:52.699
Rooney knows this, and even sees the evidence
of Ferris covering his tracks by hacking school

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:53.200
records.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:57.600
So Rooney spends the movie tracking Bueller
to prove the kid isn't really sick.

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:01.520
He goes through a lot of nonsense to catch
Bueller in the act of skipping school…which

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:04.180
means he's really just a guy trying to do
his job.

